    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37200" root="كلس" body-key="k">
    
      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كلّس</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَكْلِيسٌ</span>, <i>He plastered</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طَرَّ</span>)
a building <i>with</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِلْس</span>; as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَلَسَ</span></b> , inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَلْسٌ</span>: <i>he made smooth</i> [<i>with plaster</i>]: when a
thing is thickly plastered, it is termed <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُقَرْمَدٌ</span>.
(TA.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِلْسٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  As used by the alchemists,
[<i>He calcined</i> a substance;] <i>he dissolved</i> a body
<i>so that it became like</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كِلْس</span>. (TA.)

